From 8baf63b3f6a7df5f761501f06c7cf9da0a23c2f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <forcedinductionz@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:56:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] dmaengine: qcom: gpi: order ring memory against
 register access

gpi_read_reg() and gpi_write_reg() use the relaxed MMIO accessors for
every register, including the channel and event ring doorbells and the
event ring read pointer. The rings live in coherent DMA memory, so
nothing orders the TREs written by gpi_issue_pending() before the
doorbell that hands them to the engine, or the event ring contents after
the read pointer that says they are valid. The engine can fetch a stale
TRE, or the driver can process a stale event and complete a transfer
that is still running, which unmaps its buffer under the QUP:

  arm-smmu 15000000.iommu: Unhandled context fault: fsr=0x402, iova=0xfff5b348, fsynr=0x340003, cbfrsynra=0xca3, cb=3
  gpi a00000.dma-controller: Error in Transaction
  geni_i2c a84000.i2c: DMA txn failed:3

Use readl() and writel(), which order the register access against
normal memory.

With four readers polling the EC over this I2C bus, the fault hit
within 40 s (about 52k transfers) with only the IEOB fix applied, and
did not hit in 30 min (about 2.3M transfers) with this patch alone.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <forcedinductionz@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/EmbeddedAndroid/linux/commit/7c8b59e172a5c34db27fc1433ea935d787542150
---
 drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
index 6a47407c95b0..7584067416d6 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/qcom/gpi.c
@@ -571,12 +571,12 @@ static inline void *to_virtual(const struct gpi_ring *const ring, phys_addr_t ad
 
 static inline u32 gpi_read_reg(struct gpii *gpii, void __iomem *addr)
 {
-	return readl_relaxed(addr);
+	return readl(addr);
 }
 
 static inline void gpi_write_reg(struct gpii *gpii, void __iomem *addr, u32 val)
 {
-	writel_relaxed(val, addr);
+	writel(val, addr);
 }
 
 static __always_inline void
